content.text:
`DocumentService.archive` in `src/service.ts` now checks visibility and permission before it changes anything. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes.

- **Visibility:** a missing document, a deleted one, or one in another tenant throws `Error('not found')`. This applies to every role, admin included, and it is checked before permission.
- **Permission:** an admin may archive any visible document. An editor may archive only a document they own. A viewer never may, and any other role value is also refused. Anyone refused on a visible document gets `Error('forbidden')`.
- **Success:** it calls the existing `repository.archive`, which sets `archived` to true and appends `{actor: actor.user, document: id}` to the audit.
- **Repeat archive:** an already archived visible document does nothing, with no new audit entry. The permission check still runs first, so an unauthorized actor gets `forbidden` even then.
- **Failures:** every throw happens before any write, so documents and audit stay unchanged.

I appended a block to `checks/public.cjs` covering:
- the three not-found cases for admin and viewer;
- forbidden for an editor on someone else's document, a viewer, and an editor repeating on an already archived document they don't own;
- no changes after those failures;
- successful archives by an editor and an admin;
- an admin repeat producing no extra audit entry.

I didn't change any public interfaces.
